~ portal

Sarro: ...Liris.
Liris: I see it. It's small. Stable, though — stable like a thing that has been waiting.
Sarro: It's hers. The resonance — I've carried a scrap of her signature through forty planes. This tear answers it.
Liris: Then it goes somewhere she stood. Once. It doesn't promise more than that.
Sarro: One way to know.
Liris: Cael is ahead of us, Sarro. The gate on the other side of that wall won't wait forever. Neither will I — but I would. That's the problem.
- Go through — he has to know
	Sarro: I'll be fast. If it closes behind me, don't come after. Finish it.
	Liris: (a long silence) Come back, wayfarer.
	Sarro: ...
	Sarro: Dust. A workbench. A coil of her rope, tied off the way she always tied it — and gone on somewhere the tear couldn't follow.
	Sarro: She was here. She left. She was ALIVE to leave.
	Liris: Then that's more than you had this morning.
	Sarro: It's everything I had this morning, plus a direction. Let's go.
	do GameState.set_flag("sarro_portal", "went")
	do GameState.grant_xp(5000)
- Stay — the debt in front of us comes first
	Sarro: No. If I go through I stop being any use to anyone on this side.
	Sarro: She got out of Tamori on her own feet. She can wait one more plane for me.
	Liris: You don't have to make it sound easy.
	Sarro: It isn't. Watch the gate.
	Liris: (quietly, as the tear dims) Something shifts between them — a weight set down, or picked up. Hard to say which.
	do GameState.set_flag("sarro_portal", "stayed")
	do GameState.add_conviction(1)
	do GameState.grant_xp(5000)
=> END
